 "notes": [
  "an epsilon of 0.0 is exact equality, not a very small tolerance: no gate tolerance can be as tight, so the leg binds at every magnitude and the gate's flat regime is only the loosest place the gate ever gets",
  "at one unit of the gated quantity the gate's tolerance is already far looser than the one non-zero leg epsilon, and the crossover sits at 5e-07 units -- below any share price, so the leg is the binding test across the whole live range",
  "the flat regime is a statement about the small end of the domain, and the quantity it is rated in is not a key on either face, so the regime cannot be exercised by reading the face at all: the leaf measurement is published as a status with zero magnitudes instead of a count of unrelated numbers",
  "the crossover is published only where the gate really is `tol * x`: a row whose gate carries no scale has no crossover, and deriving one from another regime would reintroduce the unit error E313 was written to remove"
 ],
